<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- The move list, right of the board in the Wide view (1120 x 800; SceneConfig.xml): the box (760, 80) to (1080, 720), 320 x 640, as high as the board and 40 units from the right edge of the
     view; the numbers are those of Game/MovePanel.h, which says the panel is shown only while the whole box lies inside the safe area of this canvas. A canvas of the SceneView space with no
     safe area, like Material, so ChessMovePanelComponent decides what a window with insets leaves of it: in the default and the Portrait view (narrower than the box) and in a Wide window whose
     side insets cut the box (700 x 480) MovePanelBox stays hidden. Layer 5: over the pieces (0) and the result bar (1), under the HUD (10) and the panels (20); the component is listed before
     the canvas so that it gives the variables their words before the canvas draws in the same frame. Nothing here takes a click (no blocksInput, nothing interactive, not modal), so the board
     and the HUD get every press. The box is one stack on a dark plate (not a color of the board): a title band of 56 units ("Moves"), the list of 8 rows of 56 (448: the touch height the clickable
     rows of a later stage need, 32 px at the smallest Wide scale 0.6), and two bands of 56 that stay empty (MovePanelBandButtons, MovePanelBandPlayer: reserved for the takeback buttons and the
     other player's row), with 8 units between them: 56 + 8 + 448 + 8 + 56 + 8 + 56 = 640. A row is a number cell of 56 units and two cells (White's and Black's, half of the rest each); the cell of the last
     move shows its Mark, a fill in the gold of the board's last-move squares (245, 205, 50) under the text. The component writes movePanelNumber<i>, movePanelWhite<i> and movePanelBlack<i> of the
     8 rows and shows only the rows the game has (a hidden row takes no room, so the rows pack at the top); the list shows the last 8 rows of the game. The text of a move is at most 7 characters
     ("Qh4xe1+", "exd8=Q#") in a cell of 122 units, the number "100." in 56: a font of 24 and 22 units fits both at the smallest Wide scale, ChessUiTest lays the longest words out on the size matrix.
     Every name starts with MovePanel because elements are found by name in every canvas of the scene. -->
